Package: ada-unlock-uefi
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, efibootmgr, grub-common, grub2-common
Description: pre-boot Ada GPU unlock UEFI application
 Runs before Linux on headless Debian servers and applies the AD102 tensor
 unlock to every applicable RTX 4090 or L40. It can optionally select the
 64 GiB BAR1 size, then chainloads the normal Debian bootloader.
 .
 The package installs the unsigned UEFI application and its locally generated
 NVIDIA firmware payloads into the EFI System Partition, manages the matching
 UEFI boot entry, and adds pci=realloc to the GRUB command line when the 64 GiB
 BAR1 path is selected. It is intended for internal deployment only: the
 package payload contains NVIDIA firmware and must not be uploaded to a public
 archive.
